    "turn_text": "fingers in different directions. Right. So Jared would say, Oh, no, I didn't, you know, I oversaw digital, but really it was just Brad who worked on that. And Brad would say, Oh, you know, it was actually Cambridge Analytica that So everyone would point fingers at someone else as the one that was truly responsible for the digital campaign, and unless we're able to subpoena records and as a former prosecutor, for me that's where the real evidence would exist, looking at communication logs, looking at how the data was used and targeted and matching that up with what Facebook has and knows Russia did. I'll just say this though. We know now that our adversaries, Russia and God knows who else who sees this as a green light to do this. We know their capabilities. And whether you think Facebook worked with the Russians or maliciously against our democracy or not, I don't think they did. I think they were just naive. and they saw, you know, a profit motivation. Now that we know, what are we going to do about it? I think there should be a duty to report on every social media's end that if they see interference being run through their platforms, that they have to tell the FBI that doesn't exist right now. I wrote legislation that would put a duty to report on any campaign aid or candidate if you're offered information by a foreign national That is illicitly obtained you have to tell the FBI",
