  {
    "episode_id": 90451,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90451.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 151,
    "turn_text": "pass. You're going to see thousands of people who will be released who are nonviolent offenders and they'll get out of jail and have time cut off their sentences immediately. That's a good thing. Frustration for me is that in Washington, whether it's criminal justice reform, immigration or health care, we always deal with issues when they're at our doorstep and we're in crisis mode rather than when they should have been addressed. Like on immigration, we're not doing anything to address what's going on in Guatemala, Honduras, El Salvador. economically and with safety. We just wait till they come to our country and then it's wall, no wall, let them in, let them stay.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_06",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
