    "turn_text": "I was inspired to see so many people who cared about the city, like Tim Sabrani, this teacher of mine, and so many mayors and city council members over about a 10-year period. who didn't like that we had, you know, low expectations and didn't have much development in the city. And so we invested in building a new school in the town of Premier High School. We invested in attracting high-end employers by having a sales tax reimbursement program that gave back any employer that invested 50% of their sales tax. And we did smart growth instead of just putting affordable housing in one part of town. We do mixed market rate and affordable housing so that there was accountability and you couldn't just forget about affordable housing and let it go to blight. And so we now have David a Whole Foods in the town, which I think is a sign that you've made it. You know, when you have a grocery store that no one can afford to shop at, you know, we have seen it go from scrublin to Dublin. I'm proud of the work that all those leaders and I did.",
