    "turn_text": "the same way he did, which is, you know, welcome to do it. You know, I think democracy is a good thing. I actually, I think Hakeem is terrific. He's the one, he was the force in the House for this criminal justice first step bill. I mean, he worked, you know, Republicans and Democrats to get it passed. But you know, I talked to Alexandra often. I like her. I think she's a burst of energy and transparency. I was at a, I spoke at the junior state convention two weeks ago and the 14 year old who was checking me in said to me, she said, Congressman, how was your caucus vote this past week? And I looked at her and I said, How did you know that? I don't think my wife knew that we were having, you know, this caucus leadership vote. And she said, well, I follow Alexandria Acasio-Cortez on Instagram and learned how everything works. She's got millions of followers. So you've got this whole new generation that didn't really pay attention to politics, and now they're getting a window into it from her. And I think that's a benefit. Sure, there's gonna be disagreements. on policy. And my hope is that we see ourselves in this next two years as protectors, that we have to protect health care, protect paychecks, protect against corruption, and for the future of health care, energy, gun violence, that we put that and project that on the 2020 field. And we don't put ourselves in positions where we're taking tough votes, where we don't have consensus and they're going to die anyway because the Senate won't take it up or the president won't sign it. We should just protect. That's why the voters sent us here. the 2020 candidates, I think, can chart the future",
